; epsilon_compiler.delta - Delta-written direct Epsilon compiler (in progress).
;
; These retained components belong to the final compiler. They validate and
; parse the complete Epsilon surface and provide the final pure symbolic-Alpha
; encoder. The D22/D24 source-shaped semantic identity census and D31's
; complete profile-independent structural type formation are implemented. A
; source-backed catalog and ordered local-value resolution now begin the final
; checking phase; entry, remaining body/control checking, and AST-to-Alpha
; lowering remain incomplete.
; This source intentionally exposes no `main` and emits no
; placeholder artifact until those intervening phases exist.

(data EpsilonRejectReason
  (InvalidSourceByte)
  (InvalidToken)
  (InvalidCharacterLiteral)
  (UnterminatedString)
  (InvalidEscape)
  (IntegerLiteralOutOfRange)
  (UnexpectedToken)
  (UnexpectedEnd)
  (DuplicateName)
  (MissingEntry)
  (InvalidEntry)
  (InvalidBoundary)
  (UnknownType)
  (RecursiveValueType)
  (InvalidDataShape)
  (InvalidArrayLength)
  (UnknownName)
  (TypeMismatch)
  (ArityMismatch)
  (InvalidPlace)
  (UseBeforeInitialization)
  (EscapingView)
  (InvalidControlTarget)
  (InvalidTerminal)
  (DuplicatePattern)
  (NonexhaustiveSum))

(data EpsilonCompileOutcome
  (Complete Bytes)
  (Reject EpsilonRejectReason Int)
  (StorageIncompleteAt Int Int Int)
  (StorageIncompleteTotal Int Int))

; D19's sealed EpsilonCompilerV1 profile selects no boundary from these names.
; After main exists, the Delta compiler resolves this source-owned nominal
; schema and checks the complete EpsilonRejectReason-to-ECOUT-code bijection
; before it may emit the application adapter. D31/D34's two storage-refusal
; cases are the only authored path to outer Incomplete; the adapter validates
; their selected limit, requested extent, and optional source coordinate.

(data EpsilonLexicalOutcome
  (LexicallyValid)
  (LexicallyRejected EpsilonRejectReason Int))

; Native syntax values retain packed-source coordinates directly. Lists and
; optionals are recursive Delta values; no syntax node is a Bytes record or a
; numeric arena reference.
